// 2026-11-21 (landing 177d2e, row 10: DEF-720 with DEF-644's rest, DEF-691 and DEF-694's lift, form RRs; rulings l.23411, l.23500, l.23643). AN
// UNWRAP OF A POINTER IS READ TWO WAYS, BOTH KEPT: the alias pass walks a function as main does, an unwrap no step and the place under it its root
// whole, and when that walk met an unwrap of a pointer it walks the function again with every unwrap a step to its operand (the longer path, which
// re-roots through the pointer), one report per site; escape roots a view through a local's or a field's unwrap too, and an unwrap whose value is
// itself a wrapped pointer steps as well. AFA'S TWO INTERACTIONS (l.23643 items 2 and 3, ruled item 3): 12 freed reads on main and on row 10 alone
// (a10) and on T9 that are refused only on the composition, with rows 1-9 below this row. If this row fell out they would reopen; the rows land as
// one squashed commit, so no state of main shows them open.
mod:unwrap_reading_interaction_faces;
error:E5;
